<section class="page-hero"><span class="pub-kicker">Capabilities grounded in the product</span><h1>StockChief handles the work around inventory—not only inventory itself.</h1><p>These are the customer-facing capabilities present in the production PostgreSQL application. Provider-dependent areas are described with their real qualification boundaries.</p></section>
<section class="capability-catalog">
  <article><span>01</span><div><small>INVENTORY TRUTH</small><h2>Products, variants and exact balances</h2><p>Quantity, lot and serial tracking; locations; available, committed and incoming stock; counts, corrections and movement history.</p><ul><li>Negative-stock protection</li><li>Ledger reconstruction</li><li>Duplicate-event protection</li></ul></div><b class="status status--ready">Production-capable</b></article>
  <article><span>02</span><div><small>BUY &amp; RECEIVE</small><h2>Suppliers and purchasing</h2><p>Supplier items, costs, terms, reorder policy, PO approval and placement, partial or over-receipt, invoices, payments and returns.</p><ul><li>MOQ and case-pack logic</li><li>Incoming supply awareness</li><li>Invoice never silently receives stock</li></ul></div><b class="status status--ready">Production-capable</b></article>
  <article><span>03</span><div><small>MOVE</small><h2>Multi-location transfers</h2><p>Request, reserve, approve, pick, dispatch, in-transit custody, receive, variance and cancellation.</p><ul><li>Company total remains unchanged</li><li>Concurrent reservation protection</li><li>Lot and serial custody</li></ul></div><b class="status status--ready">Production-capable</b></article>
  <article><span>04</span><div><small>SELL &amp; FULFIL</small><h2>Customers and Sales Orders</h2><p>Customer records, order lines, pricing, requested dates, commitments, allocation, partial fulfillment, cancellation, returns and exchanges.</p><ul><li>Shortage consequences</li><li>Payment conditions</li><li>Physical handoff controls</li></ul></div><b class="status status--ready">Production-capable</b></article>
  <article><span>05</span><div><small>COMMUNICATE</small><h2>Business mailbox monitoring and approved sending</h2><p>Monitor a connected Gmail inbox, retain messages and send owner-approved replies or supported purchase-order templates.</p><ul><li>Approved sender filtering</li><li>Duplicate-message protection</li><li>No automatic sending authority</li></ul></div><b class="status status--limited">Provider-qualified</b></article>
  <article><span>06</span><div><small>SHIP</small><h2>Fulfillment, labels and tracking</h2><p>Compare eligible rates, purchase labels, store tracking and translate provider updates into delivery state.</p><ul><li>Destination required</li><li>Customer pickup and own-delivery paths</li><li>Exception and return statuses</li></ul></div><b class="status status--limited">Sandbox-capable</b></article>
  <article><span>07</span><div><small>COLLECT &amp; PAY</small><h2>Customer and supplier payments</h2><p>Hosted payment requests, deposits, partial and final payments, offline payments, supplier payments, refunds and payment holds.</p><ul><li>No raw card storage</li><li>Webhook idempotency</li><li>Receivable/payable reconciliation</li></ul></div><b class="status status--limited">Provider-qualified</b></article>
  <article><span>08</span><div><small>ACCOUNT</small><h2>Native books and external accounting</h2><p>Double-entry journals, inventory valuation, COGS, revenue, AP, AR, cash, expenses, reports and evidence-backed explanations.</p><ul><li>Balanced source-linked journals</li><li>Read and shadow reconciliation</li><li>Governed external posting</li></ul></div><b class="status status--ready">Core ready</b></article>
  <article><span>09</span><div><small>PLAN</small><h2>Replenishment and operating risk</h2><p>Sales-rate planning, shortages, reorder requirements, excess stock and multi-location transfer-versus-buy recommendations.</p><ul><li>Uses commitments and incoming supply</li><li>Basic stockout projections</li><li>Deterministic policy recommendations</li></ul></div><b class="status status--limited">Production-limited</b></article>
  <article><span>10</span><div><small>ASK &amp; ACT</small><h2>Ask StockChief and governed autonomy</h2><p>Ask grounded questions, explain decisions, prepare supported actions and execute inside explicit authority.</p><ul><li>Deterministic business grounding</li><li>Needs You for missing facts</li><li>Pause and resume controls</li></ul></div><b class="status status--limited">Supported domains</b></article>
</section>
